PATH RESOLUTION NOTE (no silent drift)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt's "Output" path `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Dashboard/**`
does NOT match this repository. The real, build-compiled convention (project.yml
compiles `apps/apple/Sources/**`, and every sibling P7 page — Powershare,
SleepEfficiency, Statistics, FleetCompare — lives under it) is:

    apps/apple/Sources/Features/Dashboard/**

The page was implemented there so it actually compiles into the iOS + macOS app
targets (verified: all 7 QuickStatsPage*.swift appear as SwiftCompile units in
both the macOS and iOS-Simulator builds below). `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/`
is NOT a compiled source root in project.yml; placing the file there would
produce dead, uncompiled code. Faithful interpretation of the artifact's intent
("the Dashboard feature directory"), not scope narrowing. The placeholder gate
was likewise run against the real path.

NAMING NOTE: the legacy `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/QuickStatsGrid*.swift`
(the vehicle-detail quick-stats GRID, a different surface) compiles into the same
module. All new symbols are therefore prefixed `QuickStatsPage*` to avoid
collision with the pre-existing `QuickStatsModel` / `QuickStatsStrings` /
`QuickStatsGrid` types — verified by a clean build with both trees compiled.

