IMPLEMENTATION (SwiftUI + @Observable + KMP facade; adaptive macOS + iOS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
New (apps/apple/Sources/Features/Dashboard/):
  QuickStatsPageModels.swift             value types (vehicle, summary, phase)
  QuickStatsPageFormat.swift             integer / distance(SI→unit) / energy(kWh) / currency formatters
  QuickStatsPageModel.swift              @Observable model + DataSource seam + load/refresh
  QuickStatsPageModel.Sample.swift       Sample/Empty/Failing data-source doubles
  QuickStatsPage.swift                   View: centered column + phase switch
  QuickStatsPage.Sections.swift          vehicle card, metric grid + 4 cards, footer, skeleton
  QuickStatsPageRouteRegistration.swift  registers .quickStats (+ onNavigate)
New (apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Dashboard/):
  QuickStatsPageModelTests.swift         16 XCTest cases (states/derivations/format/route)
Edited:
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift             +case quickStats (segment "quick-stats", group .overview, icon speedometer)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift             +QuickStatsPageRouteRegistration.registry(base:onNavigate:)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings     +10 keys (9 quickStats.* + route.quickStats)
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json          +2 rows (apple-macos + apple-ios, covered==required==18)

Data sources (web parity — names kept at the Swift call sites):
  useVehicles        -> GET /vehicles                      (loadVehicles; page reads vehicles?.[0])
  useVehicleState    -> GET /vehicles/{id}/state           (loadVehicleState; web stateData?.state?.state ?? 'offline')
  useAnalyticsSummary(30) -> GET /analytics/fleet?days=30  (loadSummary(days:30))
  Bound through @Observable QuickStatsPageModel (no networking in the view, ADR-004). Vehicles +
  summary are primary (web vehiclesError || analyticsError gates PageContainer error); vehicle
  state is secondary (web folds no error; defaults to 'offline'), so it degrades to nil.
SI discipline (ADR-005): the summary is stored SI-canonical — totalDistanceM (meters; web
  totalDistanceKm*1000) and energyUsedWh (watt-hours; web shows totalEnergyKwh). The view
  converts distance to the user's unit via the shared Units facade (P1/S5) and scales energy to
  kWh at the render boundary (web convertDistanceFromSI / fmtInt); nothing non-SI is stored or
  computed. Cost is a currency amount, drives a count — rendered verbatim like web.

Design note (web MetricCard `color`): the web cards pass color="cyan|green|amber|purple". Each
  Apple card keeps that semantic accent on a tinted SF Symbol (QuickStatsPageAccent →
  design-token color; purple = Color.TS.chartSeriesPower), the HIG-native equivalent of the web
  MetricCard's tinted icon container. No hardcoded colors — tokens only.

